Day 2 — Azure Networking (VNet + NSG + Load Balancer + Application Gateway)

STAR-based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your Azure application must be accessible globally with low latency and high availability. How will you design VNets, regions, and traffic routing?

2️⃣ A VM in a private subnet cannot access the internet for updates. How will you troubleshoot and fix the networking configuration?

3️⃣ You need strict network isolation between frontend, backend, and database tiers. How will you design subnets, NSGs, and routing?

4️⃣ Multiple Azure VNets across subscriptions must communicate securely. How will you implement VNet peering or hub-and-spoke architecture?

5️⃣ When will you choose Azure Load Balancer over Application Gateway, and why?

6️⃣ You need SSL termination, path-based routing, and WAF protection for a web app. How will you design this using Azure services?

7️⃣ An on-premises data center must connect securely to Azure with low latency. How will you decide between Site-to-Site VPN and ExpressRoute?

8️⃣ A service should be accessible only from specific IP ranges and countries. How will you enforce this at the network and application layer?

9️⃣ Azure Load Balancer health probes are failing even though the app is running. What troubleshooting steps will you follow?

🔟 You need private access to Azure PaaS services like Storage and SQL. How will you design this using Private Endpoints and Private DNS?

1️⃣1️⃣ Your organization wants centralized outbound internet access and inspection. How will you design routing using Azure Firewall or NVA?

1️⃣2️⃣ An application requires internal load balancing only, not public exposure. How will you configure this securely?

1️⃣3️⃣ Network traffic costs are increasing due to cross-region communication. How will you optimize architecture and routing?

1️⃣4️⃣ You need DDoS protection for a production workload. How will you design and enable Azure DDoS Protection?

1️⃣5️⃣ A DevOps team wants to enforce network rules consistently across environments. How will you implement this using IaC (ARM/Bicep/Terraform)?
